        <div class="rd-eyebrow">Individual Therapy &amp; Counseling</div>
        <div class="rd-cols">
          <div class="rd-col rd-text c1"><h2>Painful experiences as a catalyst for development</h2><p>Nobody wants to go through difficult times. And yet, in hindsight, it very often turns out:</p>
            <div class="rd-kernsatz"><p>Crisis situations are among the strongest impulses for personal development.</p></div>
            <p>Painful experiences also hold the chance to encounter ourselves anew in a profound way, to discover hidden sides and unexpected strengths within us. And, through all the effort, to develop additional abilities, strength and emotional maturity.</p></div>
          <div class="rd-clamp rd-col rd-text c2"><h2>A safe space for vulnerability</h2><p>The starting point is a trusting, professional relationship between therapist and client. Once it has developed, therapy can be a space that gives security and support. Here we may turn to our own insecurities and unpleasant sensations and learn to accept them. On our own this is usually hard, because our brain is wired to avoid the unpleasant.</p><p>Yet this is often exactly where the access lies to important, little-acknowledged needs and deep, not yet conscious longings and potentials. Perceiving, exploring and honoring them is often the prerequisite for opening up to what is new and still unknown.</p>
            <button class="rd-readmore" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span class="faq-toggle"></span><span class="rd-readmore-t">Read more</span></button>
            <p class="rd-keep"><a class="rd-more-link" href="{{ '/en/systemische-therapie/' | url }}#arbeitsverstaendnis">More on my systemic professional understanding<span class="rd-chev"></span></a></p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="snap-section rd-sec rd-tint rd-ez rd-ez-lists rd-mtabs" id="anlaesse" data-index="2">
      <div class="about-band offers-band"></div>
      <div class="rd-inner">
        <div class="rd-eyebrow">Individual Therapy &amp; Counseling</div>
        <div class="rd-mtabbar" role="tablist"><button class="is-active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-mtab="0">Occasions</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-mtab="1">How it helps</button></div>
        <div class="rd-cols">
          <div class="rd-col rd-text c1 rd-mpanel is-active" data-mpanel="0"><h2>What can be occasions for individual therapy?</h2>
            <ul class="rd-bullets">
              <li>The wish to understand yourself and your relationships more deeply</li>
              <li>Stressful life events, or the feeling that certain problems keep repeating</li>
              <li>Sudden changes, for example at work, in your living situation, through illness or separation</li>
              <li>Distressing feelings or strong inner uncertainty</li>
              <li>Inner blockages or the wish for orientation and new meaning</li>
              <li>No clear occasion, and yet something has been thrown off balance or your self-image has been shaken</li>
            </ul></div>
          <div class="rd-col rd-text c2 rd-mpanel" data-mpanel="1"><h2>What can individual therapy help with?</h2>
            <ul class="rd-bullets">
              <li>Finding orientation in stressful life situations and difficult relationships</li>
              <li>Recognizing unhelpful patterns of thinking, feeling and behavior and developing helpful alternatives</li>
              <li>Feeling emotions, including unpleasant ones, more clearly and handling them and conflicts with greater confidence</li>
              <li>Perceiving your own needs and longings, strengthening self-worth and unfolding potentials</li>
              <li>Sensing what feels right for you, standing up for boundaries and developing a sustainable self-image</li>
              <li>Developing concrete steps toward the change you want</li>
            </ul></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

